{"name":"Ballyhoo","hex":"#58a83b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ballyhoo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sensational or clamorous advertising or publicity.","Noisy shouting or uproar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sensationalize or make grand claims."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballyhoo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballyhoo","blocks":[{"text":"The ballyhoo halfbeak, ballyhoo, balahu, redtailed balao or yellowtail ballyhoo is a baitfish of the halfbeak family (Hemiramphidae). It is similar to the Balao halfbeak in most features. Some are used for trolling by saltwater anglers. Some have caused ciguatera poisoning in humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hemiramphus_brasiliensis_distribution_map.jpg/330px-Hemiramphus_brasiliensis_distribution_map.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballyhoo","wikidata":"Q515014"},{"title":"Ballyhoo (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Ballyhoo is an interactive fiction game designed by Jeff O'Neill and published by Infocom in 1985. The circus-themed game was released for ten systems, including MS-DOS, Atari ST, and Commodore 64. Ballyhoo was labeled as \"Standard\" difficulty. It is Infocom's nineteenth game."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0e/Ballyhoo_box_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballyhoo_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q805415"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Halfbeak_Cuba.JPG/500px-Halfbeak_Cuba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Halfbeak_Cuba.JPG/1280px-Halfbeak_Cuba.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu